%% DM26-0670

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Domain as Domain actor<br/>(ClusterWatcher, AttestationSupervisor)
    participant Handler as ProtocolActor
    participant Task as Kubernetes::perform<br/>(its own task)
    participant API as Kubernetes API
    participant Read as operation.read<br/>(a blocking thread)
    participant Broker as Cassini client

    Note over Domain,Broker: As built, 2026-11-04 (docs/architecture/protocol-handlers.md). A watch never ends, so one request has many results. Each is a message, and the next waits for the last.

    Domain->>Handler: stream(operation, myself, wrap)
    Handler-->>Domain: a Streaming, which ends it when dropped
    Handler->>Handler: judge (Location::Cluster): TLS, no host of the domain's,<br/>recorded with credential=service-account
    Handler->>Task: perform(watch)
    activate Task
    Task->>API: list, with the pod's own token (kube reads and renews its file)
    API-->>Task: the objects, then a watch

    loop each change: Listing, Applied, Deleted, Listed
        Task->>Read: read(change)
        activate Read
        alt it reads
            Read-->>Task: a value
            deactivate Read
            Task->>Domain: Seen(Delivery with Ok(value))
            activate Domain
            opt the observer: a publish that waits for room
                Domain->>Broker: publish_when_ready
                Broker-->>Domain: there is room
            end
            Domain-->>Task: finished with the message, so the Delivery goes
            deactivate Domain
            Note over Task,Read: The next change is not read until then,<br/>so a broker falling behind slows this watch and no other.
        else it does not
            Read-->>Task: Malformed
            Task->>Domain: Seen(Delivery with Err): its last word
            Note over Domain,Task: A stream says each change once, so a gap ends it.
        end
    end

    alt the API refused (403) or does not serve the kind (404)
        API-->>Task: Status
        Task->>Domain: Seen(Delivery with Err(Configuration)): its last word
        Note over Domain,Task: Attestation: what it holds is no longer whole, it cannot say,<br/>and it asks again in 5 s. The observer asks again in 5 minutes.
    else the watch is lost
        API-->>Task: an error, or the connection goes
        Task->>Domain: Seen(Delivery with Err(Transient)): its last word
        Note over Domain,Task: Each asks again in 5 s. No retries in a handler: the new<br/>watch starts from a list, so what was missed is said again.
    else the domain drops its Streaming, as for a namespace that has gone
        Domain->>Task: dropped
        Note over Domain,Task: The task ends where it is, and nothing follows.
    end
    deactivate Task
